  "evidence": "TEXT_D: +£540m yearly for NHS, restore free eye/dental checks, cut waits to 6 months, stronger carers’ support and fairer long‑term care; end rough sleeping by 2000, build more affordable homes, bring empty homes back into use, strengthen tenants’ rights; universal early‑years education for 3–4 year‑olds, cut primary classes to ≤30, income‑linked student repayments, Individual Learning Accounts; raise personal allowance and introduce a 50% rate over £100k, minimum wage (regionally varied), childcare strategy, measures to break poverty traps; strengthen anti‑discrimination (Human Rights Commission, equal age of consent, repeal Section 28, tackle racism, civil rights for disabled). TEXT_F: keep taxes low (20p basic, 40p top), limit government to <40% of GDP, oppose EU Social Chapter and a national minimum wage; welfare‑to‑work with firm obligations; more police/CCTV, mandatory minimum sentences; sovereignty and NATO‑first/nuclear deterrent; NHS real‑terms increases and support for carers; education focus on testing, discipline, and more grammar schools.",
